<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Panagiotis Danglis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1853">1853</a>–<a href="/years/1924">1924</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Panagiotis Danglis was a Greek army general and politician, known for designing the Schneider-Danglis mountain gun, who served as chief of staff to Crown Prince Constantine in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a>. In 1916 he formed, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleftherios-venizelos">Eleftherios Venizelos</a> and Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pavlos-kountouriotis">Pavlos Kountouriotis</a>, the triumvirate that led the Provisional Government of National Defence at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessaloniki</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/panagiotis-danglis.jpg" alt="Panagiotis Danglis" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agence Rol · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%A9n%C3%A9ral_Danglis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
